  "evidence": "Manifest 0xc54d214 registers the main page. The create callback installs the list callback table at 0x200d3514 and calls list refresh before setting 0x201130a0; descriptor root is used as active guard. Row create and update register callback 0xc56654c, with filters 0 and 7 respectively. The callback reads event code and index, then loads a destination from one of the two tables. Destination 0x20001 is handled specially as an app navigation request rather than an ordinary page ID.",
  "scope": "The two recovered row tables and the four listed event call sites; indices describe static order, with two layouts selected by sub_C4BF490. The nonzero table documents its first nine rows; actual count is 10 minus the byte returned by sub_C4BF490.",
  "limitations": "Returned row index is used for indexed table access without a local bounds check; changing it to an invalid value can crash. Menu arrays contain app/page destinations, not verified public API IDs. Page slots do not prove thread quiescence, and true event behavior and recovery require device testing.",
